<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <PackageId>BulletMLLib</PackageId>
    <Version>5.1.3</Version>
    <Title>BulletMLLib</Title>
    <Authors>dmanning23</Authors>
    <description>Library for parsing BulletML xml files. Used for scripting bullet patterns in shmup games.</description>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/dmanning23/BulletMLLib</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/dmanning23/BulletMLLib</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>monogame</PackageTags>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
5.1.3

Recursive actions work. An action can now reference itself, directly or through other actions, as long as it reaches a wait before it recurses. 5.1 rejected every such pattern as a "circular actionRef".
- When the recursive actionRef is the last thing left to run, the action restarts with the new params instead of nesting another copy of itself, so a pattern can recurse for as long as the game runs without using more memory or stack.
- A cycle with no wait would loop forever in one frame, so it still fails to load: The action node "loop" has a circular actionRef with no wait before it
- If a recursive action's waits come out as 0 at runtime (for example $rand*2), it runs once per frame instead of hanging.

Upgrading from 5.0? 5.1.0 made pattern validation much stricter. See the full release notes before upgrading.

Full release notes: https://github.com/dmanning23/BulletMLLib/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="MonoGame.Framework.DesktopGL" Version="3.8.*">
      <PrivateAssets>All</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="Vector2Extensions" Version="5.*"/>
    <PackageReference Include="Equationator" Version="5.*"/>
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>